# WhitePact release-signing allowed signers file.
#
# Git SSH-signature "allowed signers" format (see `git help gpg-sign` /
# ssh-keygen(1) "ALLOWED SIGNERS" section):
#
#   <principal> <key-type> <base64-public-key>
#
# One line per approved release signer. `<principal>` should be a
# stable identifier for the person (e.g. their email), not a
# description. Example (illustrative only — not a real key):
#
#   founder@whitepact.com ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAI...
#
# CRITICAL: this file holds PUBLIC keys only. Never paste a private
# key (anything from `~/.ssh/id_*` without the `.pub` suffix, or a
# PEM block containing "PRIVATE KEY") into this file or anywhere else
# in this repository.
#
# Status as of 2026-08-19 (see compliance/SIGNED_VERSION_TAGS.md):
# NO SIGNER IS CONFIGURED YET. This file intentionally contains no
# key material below this line. The release workflow's
# `verify-signed-tag` job treats an empty/placeholder-only file as a
# hard failure — every tag is rejected, not silently accepted,
# until a real founder/maintainer public key is added here.
#
# To add yourself as an approved release signer:
#   1. Generate or locate your SSH signing key (RELEASING.md "One-time
#      setup: SSH tag signing" has the exact commands).
#   2. Append one line here in the format above, using your PUBLIC
#      key (the `.pub` file's contents) — never the private key.
#   3. Open a PR. This file changing is itself a security-sensitive
#      change and should be reviewed like one.
